BookShop POS Details:

This is a simplified POS for bookshop owners to easily keep track of stock levels and sales. The plan is to implement a printing function for on the spot receipts to avoid having to manually write down the customer's order.
There will be a feature to be able to pull the days total sales to then send to the finance manager.

Later down the line the EFTPOS sale functionality will also hopefully be functional.









Roadmap

Item Admin Screen - Add/edit/delete items and adjust stock through the UI, using the skeleton and ItemDao stubs just provided.
 This unblocks entering your real catalog instead of editing SQL by hand.

Sales History / Retrieval Screen - A screen listing past sales for a given day,
drilling into each one's line items. Reuses the same TableView pattern as the item admin screen, so it's good next practice.

Receipt Printer Output - Pick a specific USB ESC/POS thermal printer model (e.g. Epson TM-T20III),
then integrate a library like JavaPOS or a plain ESC/POS command sender to print itemized receipts with GST breakdown on checkout.

Stocktake Tool - A daily stock count screen: enter counted quantities,
compare against system stock, and an override to redo the count if needed.
Consider allowing a second count for safety as the manager requested.

End of Day Summary - Generate a PDF of the day's total sales and email it automatically to the business/store manager.
 Needs a PDF library (e.g. OpenPDF) and an email library (JavaMail) with SMTP details for whichever email account will send it.

Real EFTPOS Integration - Once a payment provider/terminal is chosen (e.g. Tyro, Windcave),
integrate their SDK so checkout triggers an actual terminal transaction instead of just marking payment method manually.

Final Polishing and handover - Error handling for edge cases, a backup strategy for the database file,
and packaging the app as a proper installable (e.g. via jpackage) so user can launch it without opening IntelliJ or a terminal.